#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Study system helper.

  study new <Subject>            create a subject folder from _template
  study ingest <Subject>         convert new materials into converted/*.md
  study ingest <Subject> --url URL   download a lecture video (yt-dlp), then ingest
  study list                     list subjects
  study index <Subject>          (re)build the semantic index over converted/
  study search <Subject> <query> [-k N]   find the most relevant passages
  study ask <Subject> <question>  answer now if grounded, else queue it for when you're online
  study tutor <Subject> [message]  local orchestrator: with a message, one turn; without, an
                                   interactive session (both models kept warm between questions)
  study queue <Subject>          list the deferred (escalation) questions still pending
  study drain <Subject>          if online, let Claude (headless CLI) clear the queue into cards/
  study watch <Subject>          run in the background: auto-drain the moment the connection returns
  study resolve <Subject> <id>   write a resolved answer (from stdin) into cards/, mark it done
  study cards <Subject>          show the cards built from resolved (escalated) questions
  study doctor                   check hardware + tools, recommend a search mode (changes nothing)
  study setup [--mode auto|cpu|off]   install semantic search (default: the recommended mode)

Deferred escalation (offline-first): `ask` runs locally. A question that is not grounded in your
materials, or that needs real reasoning, is not answered with a weak guess — it goes into
<Subject>/queue.jsonl. `drain` checks connectivity and, when online, bundles the pending questions
for the strong model; resolved answers land as cards in <Subject>/cards/.

Semantic search is optional (see .tools/semantic.py): llama.cpp + a 310 MB model, ~330 MB in all,
no Python packages. Once set up, ingest refreshes the index automatically. The index lives in
.tools/index/<Subject>/, the chosen mode in .tools/config.json.

Conversion (skips files already converted and unchanged):
  .pdf                  -> pdftotext, with '--- page N ---' markers; pages without a text layer
                           (scans) are OCR'd: Apple Vision on macOS (.tools/ocr.swift), else tesseract.
                           STUDY_OCR_LANGS overrides the language (Vision: ja-JP,en-US; tesseract: jpn+eng)
  .pptx .docx .xlsx     -> markitdown (slides keep '<!-- Slide number: N -->')
  .mp4 .mov .mkv .webm .m4a .mp3 .wav
                        -> ffmpeg + whisper.cpp, with [hh:mm:ss] timestamps
  .md .txt              -> copied as is
"""

